WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.078
Home Repairs and Services.

2
00:00:02.358 --> 00:00:06.411
Day 50 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.161 --> 00:00:09.185
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:19.129
Today's goal: explain a problem to a plumber, electrician or technician, agree on the cost before work starts, and give clear instructions to house help.

5
00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:21.333
Part 1.

6
00:00:21.613 --> 00:00:22.573
Key words.

7
00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.188
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:47.036
Word or phrase, and Meaning. leak or drip or blocked or clogged: water problems. short circuit or tripped or no power or spark: electrical problems. geyser or water heater or RO or purifier: appliances. service or repair or replace or spare part: the work. visiting charge or labour charge: fee for

9
00:00:47.316 --> 00:00:56.873
coming or for work. warranty or AMC (annual maintenance contract): covered repairs. house help or cook or driver: domestic staff.

10
00:00:58.223 --> 00:00:59.098
Part 2.

11
00:00:59.378 --> 00:01:00.786
Describing the problem.

12
00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:03.572
The kitchen tap is leaking.

13
00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:05.175
It started yesterday.

14
00:01:05.455 --> 00:01:07.311
I tightened it, but it still drips.

15
00:01:07.591 --> 00:01:09.468
The bedroom AC isn't cooling.

16
00:01:09.748 --> 00:01:11.711
It turns on, but the air is warm.

17
00:01:11.991 --> 00:01:13.740
It was serviced six months ago.

18
00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.687
The power trips every time we switch on the geyser.

19
00:01:18.037 --> 00:01:18.933
Part 3.

20
00:01:19.213 --> 00:01:20.429
Questions you'll ask.

21
00:01:21.679 --> 00:01:23.193
What's the visiting charge?

22
00:01:23.473 --> 00:01:25.841
Can you tell me the total cost before you start?

23
00:01:26.121 --> 00:01:27.209
What's the problem?

24
00:01:27.489 --> 00:01:29.879
Can it be repaired, or does it need replacing?

25
00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:31.716
Is the spare part original?

26
00:01:31.996 --> 00:01:33.809
Is there a warranty on the repair?

27
00:01:34.089 --> 00:01:35.369
How long will it take?

28
00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:38.508
Can you come tomorrow morning between 9 and 11?

29
00:01:38.788 --> 00:01:40.303
Can I pay by UPI?

30
00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:41.692
Could I have a bill?

31
00:01:43.042 --> 00:01:43.959
Part 4.

32
00:01:44.239 --> 00:01:46.906
Conversation 1: booking an AC repair.

33
00:01:48.156 --> 00:01:50.183
Here is how the conversation goes.

34
00:01:50.463 --> 00:01:52.425
CoolCare service, how can I help?

35
00:01:52.705 --> 00:01:55.052
Hi, my split AC isn't cooling.

36
00:01:55.332 --> 00:01:57.295
It runs, but the air is warm.

37
00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:59.473
Which brand and how old is it?

38
00:01:59.753 --> 00:02:02.143
It's a Daikin, about three years old.

39
00:02:02.423 --> 00:02:04.065
When was it last serviced?

40
00:02:05.415 --> 00:02:07.015
The conversation continues.

41
00:02:07.295 --> 00:02:08.959
About eight months ago.

42
00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:10.925
It may need a gas refill.

43
00:02:11.205 --> 00:02:16.303
The visiting charge is 399, rupeesand that's adjusted in the final bill.

44
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:18.930
How much is a gas refill, roughly?

45
00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:24.799
Between 2,500 rupeesand 3,500, rupeesdepending on the leak.

46
00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:26.018
Okay.

47
00:02:26.298 --> 00:02:29.477
Can the technician come tomorrow between 10 and 12?

48
00:02:30.827 --> 00:02:32.427
The conversation continues.

49
00:02:32.707 --> 00:02:34.072
Yes, I've booked it.

50
00:02:34.352 --> 00:02:36.464
The technician will call you before coming.

51
00:02:36.744 --> 00:02:37.683
Thank you.

52
00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:39.993
Part 5.

53
00:02:40.273 --> 00:02:42.534
Conversation 2: with the technician.

54
00:02:43.784 --> 00:02:45.811
Here is how the conversation goes.

55
00:02:46.091 --> 00:02:47.563
The gas is very low.

56
00:02:47.843 --> 00:02:49.955
There's a small leak near the pipe joint.

57
00:02:50.235 --> 00:02:53.733
Can you fix the leak, or will you only refill the gas?

58
00:02:54.013 --> 00:02:56.168
I'll fix the joint first, then refill.

59
00:02:56.448 --> 00:02:58.240
What will the total cost be?

60
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.104
3,200, rupeesincluding the visiting charge.

61
00:03:03.454 --> 00:03:05.054
The conversation continues.

62
00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.403
Is there a warranty on the work?

63
00:03:07.683 --> 00:03:09.603
Three months on the leak repair.

64
00:03:09.883 --> 00:03:11.547
Okay, please go ahead.

65
00:03:11.827 --> 00:03:13.662
Could you also clean the filters?

66
00:03:13.942 --> 00:03:15.670
Yes, no extra charge.

67
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:16.697
Great.

68
00:03:16.977 --> 00:03:19.878
Please send me the bill on WhatsApp after you finish.

69
00:03:21.228 --> 00:03:22.167
Part 6.

70
00:03:22.447 --> 00:03:25.177
Instructions to house help (clear and respectful).

71
00:03:26.427 --> 00:03:28.411
Could you please clean the balcony today?

72
00:03:28.691 --> 00:03:30.867
Also, the bedsheets need to be washed.

73
00:03:31.147 --> 00:03:33.643
Please don't use this cleaner on the wooden table.

74
00:03:33.923 --> 00:03:35.331
Use the cloth instead.

75
00:03:35.611 --> 00:03:38.747
We'll be away from Friday to Monday, so you don't need to come.

76
00:03:39.027 --> 00:03:40.542
Your salary won't be cut.

77
00:03:40.822 --> 00:03:42.593
Thank you, the kitchen looks great.

78
00:03:43.943 --> 00:03:44.881
Part 7.

79
00:03:45.161 --> 00:03:46.079
Practice.

80
00:03:47.329 --> 00:03:52.150
Describe a problem at home using: what + where + since when + what you've tried.

81
00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.375
Part 8.

82
00:03:54.655 --> 00:03:55.700
Speak today.

83
00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:00.833
Practise asking What will the total cost be? before agreeing to any work.

84
00:04:01.113 --> 00:04:03.993
Give one clear, polite instruction at home in English.

85
00:04:05.343 --> 00:04:06.879
That's the end of this lesson.

86
00:04:07.159 --> 00:04:11.831
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

87
00:04:12.111 --> 00:04:18.212
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

